{"repositoryId":1209462089,"availability":"available","full":"localangle/backfield","name":"backfield","description":"An open platform for turning journalism into data you can build with","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":25,"forks":1,"created":"2026-04-13T13:01:28Z","updated":"2026-10-12T18:47:52Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://localangle.co","topics":[],"demo":"https://try.backfield.news/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.269Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.269Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.269Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.269Z","stars":25,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An open platform for turning journalism into data you can build with","Learn more &bull; Try it &bull; Documentation &bull; Cookbook &bull; Self-Hosting","Backfield turns unstructured news stories into structured data at scale. Among other things, it extracts and geocodes the locations of news events; organizes people and their quotes; and connects people, places and organizations into a living knowledge graph based on your coverage."],"features":["Creating geographically targeted news feeds that surface parts of articles relevant to readers in different cities and neighborhoods. If your neighborhood coffee shop is mentioned in paragraph 20 of a long story, you'll…","Annotating articles with complex taxonomies, such as user needs and story formats, for the purpose of enriching analytics.","Building knowledge graphs from years of news archives, which can be used to power sophisticated and explainable AI search systems.","Pulling apart narrative stories, such as recipes and obituaries, into structured data for the purposes of building new products and story forms.","Mapping a newsroom's coverage geographically, auditing sources, and otherwise providing a high-level view of community coverage."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/locala